
### 1. Create a course
POST http://localhost:3002/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Programming Fundamentals",
  "code": "CS101",
  "credits": 3,
  "description": "Introduction to programming"
}

###

### 2. Get all courses
GET http://localhost:3002/courses

###

### 3. Get course by ID
GET http://localhost:3002/courses/1

###

### 4. Update course
PUT http://localhost:3002/courses/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Advanced Programming",
  "credits": 4
}

###

### 5. Delete course
DELETE http://localhost:3002/courses/1

###

### 6. Test invalid credits (should return 400)
POST http://localhost:3002/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Database Systems",
  "code": "CS202",
  "credits": 5
}

###

### 7. Test missing required name (should return 400)
POST http://localhost:3002/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "CS303",
  "credits": 3
}

###
POST http://localhost:3002/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Programming Fundamentals",
  "code": "CS101",
  "credits": 3,
  "description": "Introduction to programming"
}
### 8. Create a valid database course
POST http://localhost:3002/courses
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Database Systems",
  "code": "CS202",
  "credits": 3,
  "description": "Introduction to databases"
}

### Final course list
GET http://localhost:3002/courses